# kills: no deck chip ever rests under + ADD, at any width, state or scroll
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^no.deck.chip.ever.rests.under...ADD..at.any.width..state.or.scroll$ tests/e2e.test.js
# + ADD stops travelling with the strip and is pinned to its left edge on top
# of the row. It is then still fully on screen - rects alone see nothing wrong
# - but deck chips scroll to rest underneath it: elementFromPoint at a visible
# chip returns the button, so tapping "D AMARA 9" opens the create sheet
# instead of switching decks. That is the mis-tap normal flow prevents.
